# What a shared wire delivers when something is wrong. Each record names the
# failure; none may panic. A value of the wrong length still decodes as an
# element and round-trips, so it can be inspected; only its meaning fails.

44 42 90 => error truncated 5/3
f9 => error truncated 2/1
65 => error truncated 2/1
65 fe 00 => error truncated 4/3
46 => error reserved-lvt 6
0e 21 48 => error unbalanced
0f => error unbalanced
0e 1f => error unbalanced
43 42 90 00 => real invalid
12 => boolean invalid
82 08 a8 => bits invalid
81 01 => bits invalid
82 01 => error truncated 3/2
20 => unsigned invalid
95 05 01 00 00 00 00 => enumerated invalid
